## Code Example
```javascript
// OpenTelemetry configuration for CNPA pipeline
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { HttpInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-http');
const { PgInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-pg');
const { RedisInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-redis');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  instrumentations: [
    new HttpInstrumentation(),
    new PgInstrumentation(),
    new RedisInstrumentation()
  ],
  serviceName: 'cnpa-service'
});

// Kafka context propagation example
const produceWithTracing = async (topic, message, span) => {
  const headers = {
    traceparent: span.spanContext().traceparent,
    'x-request-id': span.spanContext().traceId
  };
  await producer.send({ topic, messages: [{ value: message, headers }] });
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Advanced multi-region CNPA scenarios demand precise fault-localization across HTTP, DB, Kafka, and cross-region replication. This question probes systematic debugging, observability design, and practical fixes that preserve data integrity and latency.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region Kafka replication and lag diagnosis
- End-to-end tracing across services
- Producer batching, acks, and idempotent writes
- Failover testing and impact assessment

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: add a tracing span around HTTP handler to trace end-to-end latency
const tracer = require('@opentelemetry/api');

app.post('/api/events', async (req, res) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http.handle-events');
  try {
    // Business logic here
    await processEvent(req.body);
    res.status(200).json({ success: true });
  } catch (error) {
    span.recordException(error);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Processing failed' });
  } finally {
    span.end();
  }
});
```
